#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105511 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a087e7bc-4e74-584d-af3b-bf6bee4b75ea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Their Components"}] :question/id #uuid "3d38f3e0-4c27-5ac6-ac16-9c8f57e0000e" :question/math-academy-id "e-4327" :question/problem "Find the angle between $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 2,-1,1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 1,5,-2 \\rangle$. Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." :question/worked-solution "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 5+1\\cdot (-2)}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-5}{\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{30}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-5}{\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta = \\arccos \\left( -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{6} \\right) \\approx 111.9^\\circ.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105512 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7b1b8dc-bb50-59b4-8716-bdd6fbeada4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Three Points"}] :question/id #uuid "d6d1be58-7321-50ca-a47d-5e80d55277c3" :question/math-academy-id "e-4328" :question/problem "Find $\\angle BAC$ given the points $A(2,-1,-5)$, $B(-1,0,-4)$, and $C(5,1,1).$ Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A$, $B$, $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨2,-1,-5⟩,\\,b=⟨-1,0,-4⟩,\\,c=⟨5,1,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $\\triangle ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $\\angle BAC = \\theta.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,-4⟩-⟨2,-1,-5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,1,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨5,1,1⟩-⟨2,-1,-5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,2,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3\\cdot 3+1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 6}{\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{6}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1}{\\sqrt{11}\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{7\\sqrt{11}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta = \\arccos \\left( -\\dfrac{1}{7\\sqrt{11}} \\right) \\approx 92.5^\\circ.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105529 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a418d9aa-d74d-58b1-a4c9-819f63593d50" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given the Value of Their Dot Product"}] :question/id #uuid "fb2df468-d70d-5300-8860-0cb729cb13c5" :question/math-academy-id "e-5112" :question/problem "Given that $\\mathbf{a}\\cdot \\mathbf{b}=-4$, find the angle between $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle t, \\, -2 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 6, \\, t \\rangle$. Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." :question/worked-solution "First, since $\\mathbf{a}\\cdot \\mathbf{b}=-4$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =-4 \\\\ t\\cdot 6+(-2)\\cdot t & =-4 \\\\ 6t-2t & =-4 \\\\ 4t & =-4 \\\\ t & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨-1,-2⟩,\\,b=⟨6,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-2)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{6}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{37}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{185}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta = \\arccos \\left( -\\dfrac{4}{\\sqrt{185}} \\right) \\approx 107.1^\\circ.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186325324 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a087e7bc-4e74-584d-af3b-bf6bee4b75ea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Their Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb997459-1c05-5493-973d-0e89478a67e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{91.7}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325326} {:answer/id #uuid "ce46609d-1539-5250-978a-3c0846a2b548" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{102.1}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325327} {:answer/id #uuid "c4a32a1d-55b0-5423-b6cc-d008ab997367" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{94.6}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325328} {:answer/id #uuid "a1f60648-fa54-5c56-aca9-55b17eae8093" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{89.9}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325329} {:answer/id #uuid "6841f3bc-de1d-573c-8373-e481429455dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{85.6}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325330}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4a32a1d-55b0-5423-b6cc-d008ab997367" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{94.6}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325328} :answer-field/id #uuid "79d36258-e554-53c0-a410-c65dbdecabce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325325}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "068e8007-9b15-5291-bff1-582a2d3f3df4" :question/math-academy-id "q-101501" :question/problem "Find the angle between $a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." :question/worked-solution "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 4+(-6)\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-6)^{2}}\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{37}\\cdot \\sqrt{17}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{629}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{629}})≈{94.6}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186325331 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a087e7bc-4e74-584d-af3b-bf6bee4b75ea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Their Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ceece46-3fc8-540c-b050-d10cf1f0c6b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{85.09}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325333} {:answer/id #uuid "7200eebe-b8b7-5bef-8986-98b60860efff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{80.13}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325334} {:answer/id #uuid "d8b7e83e-1e78-5493-9b1b-5f5f0a8dc9fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{77.11}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325335} {:answer/id #uuid "6fc39dd4-f2d0-5981-959d-08bf86fb316f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{83.21}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325336} {:answer/id #uuid "9e405340-a8a0-5819-a80c-aa3e7c6f426b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{78.56}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325337}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7200eebe-b8b7-5bef-8986-98b60860efff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{80.13}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325334} :answer-field/id #uuid "33102697-50b6-5b38-88af-cdf9060ee2ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325332}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "48a4942c-3458-5abb-8ba9-d5e046195ced" :question/math-academy-id "q-101505" :question/problem "Find the angle between $a=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\cdot 3+0\\cdot 6+6\\cdot (-2)}{\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{6}^{2}}\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{6}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{100}\\cdot \\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{10\\cdot 7} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{35}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{6}{35})≈{80.13}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269073 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7b1b8dc-bb50-59b4-8716-bdd6fbeada4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Three Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb1e08c5-8191-51cb-828c-4e1bf4d18edb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{79}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269075} {:answer/id #uuid "c48d61db-8a7b-58a9-baa3-b45f0e2b2e24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{77}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269076} {:answer/id #uuid "6fe43b6a-8e20-5aa9-b47c-1e0b409544b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{86}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269077} {:answer/id #uuid "a8481d0e-1847-5899-a263-24206ff622f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{91}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269078} {:answer/id #uuid "f68369eb-d5b2-597a-8ad3-4e02ef54893c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{81}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269079}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6fe43b6a-8e20-5aa9-b47c-1e0b409544b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{86}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269077} :answer-field/id #uuid "4237779a-fb1d-5aae-9935-ca22c819fe5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269074}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "16a09fd3-be95-51b4-b0ac-0c24039ae9ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-101511" :question/problem "Find $∠BAC$ given the points $A(2,-1,1)$, $B(3,1,-2)$, and $C(-1,1,1).$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A$, $B$, $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨2,-1,1⟩,\\,b=⟨3,1,-2⟩,\\,c=⟨-1,1,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨3,1,-2⟩-⟨2,-1,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,2,-3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨-1,1,1⟩-⟨2,-1,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,2,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (-3)+2\\cdot 2+(-3)\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-3)^{2}}\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{14}\\cdot \\sqrt{13}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{182}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{182}})≈{86}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305573 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a418d9aa-d74d-58b1-a4c9-819f63593d50" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given the Value of Their Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe092e6a-a292-562a-8e10-3a18cf911c21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{150}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305575} {:answer/id #uuid "9012605f-9225-5ab8-adaf-c6233a381fab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{90}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305576} {:answer/id #uuid "cd96dcf2-df7b-5d7d-b63a-2f885d7a0ef4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{180}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305577} {:answer/id #uuid "a6c459a6-1bf4-521f-b918-6d61ed3c3273" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{135}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305578} {:answer/id #uuid "5a531894-930d-5aa8-be0a-b7eeb2655660" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{120}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6c459a6-1bf4-521f-b918-6d61ed3c3273" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{135}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305578} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7d14433-e6bf-53f2-aba4-b6c9efded31e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305574}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0fe38227-7ce9-5330-a6c3-677c59d25bae" :question/math-academy-id "q-101512" :question/problem "Given that $a\\cdot b=-5$, find the angle between $a=⟨2t,t⟩$ and $b=⟨1,3⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $a\\cdot b=-5$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =-5 \\\\ 2t\\cdot 1+t\\cdot 3 & =-5 \\\\ 2t+3t & =-5 \\\\ 5t & =-5 \\\\ t & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =⟨2(-1),\\,(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $a$ and $b$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-5}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{10}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{5\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}})={135}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186325338 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a418d9aa-d74d-58b1-a4c9-819f63593d50" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given the Value of Their Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf1a3d83-c0d0-5d59-a725-a4e550616531" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{40.5}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325340} {:answer/id #uuid "345b08c5-cf95-54c0-961f-48ebefe29864" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{42.3}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325341} {:answer/id #uuid "15b71257-302d-58eb-b6d6-a575553f86d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45.1}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325342} {:answer/id #uuid "61964971-6f18-575d-bb4c-ec4324e66d09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{44.4}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325343} {:answer/id #uuid "f43dd61c-e951-51e1-b3f0-81494fd85fe5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{39.9}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325344}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "345b08c5-cf95-54c0-961f-48ebefe29864" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{42.3}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325341} :answer-field/id #uuid "885fe984-e9dc-55cb-800b-ef3684faddb7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325339}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6924e182-afff-5ad5-8eac-9fcb60a7b5ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-101515" :question/problem "Given that $p\\cdot q=11$, find the angle between $p=⟨t,t-1⟩$ and $q=⟨-4,-1⟩.$ Round your answer to $1$ decimal place." :question/worked-solution "First, since $p\\cdot q=11$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & =11 \\\\ t\\cdot (-4)+(t-1)\\cdot (-1) & =11 \\\\ -4t-t+1 & =11 \\\\ -5t & =10 \\\\ t & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨(-2),(-2)-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $p$ and $q$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{p\\cdot q}{|\\,p\\,||\\,q\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{p}_{x}{q}_{x}+{p}_{y}{q}_{y}}{\\sqrt{{p}_{x}^{2}+{p}_{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{{q}_{x}^{2}+{q}_{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-3)^{2}}\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{13}\\cdot \\sqrt{17}} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{221}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{221}})≈{42.3}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305587 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7b1b8dc-bb50-59b4-8716-bdd6fbeada4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Three Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b799d246-a11b-5070-8463-6dd43a31f2fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{23}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305589} {:answer/id #uuid "0efd139f-2138-5c6a-8e89-f0113b4b5529" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{25}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305590} {:answer/id #uuid "5e90994a-68d7-554e-8846-e8e826dcaf09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{28}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305591} {:answer/id #uuid "77dbf72a-adae-5231-b827-7a1763244fb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305592} {:answer/id #uuid "a49f55ad-0b4a-59d1-9d05-998e90849253" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{21}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0efd139f-2138-5c6a-8e89-f0113b4b5529" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{25}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305590} :answer-field/id #uuid "45442419-9910-5c12-9801-3473e30f7e7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305588}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2da436d8-ed5e-54f6-ba9e-01977eb421f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-124826" :question/problem "Find $∠XZY$ given the points $X(-2,1,0)$, $Y(-1,0,4)$, and $Z(-1,2,-2).$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $X$, $Y$, $Z$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=⟨-2,1,0⟩,\\,y=⟨-1,0,4⟩,\\,z=⟨-1,2,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $△XYZ$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠XZY=\\theta .$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/assets/87453fecb9da6b9e673ab5a85a289a3fac73f4fb90fc8f1b33e7c0a80b1ea77f.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{ZX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{ZY}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{ZX} & =x-z \\\\  & =⟨-2,1,0⟩-⟨-1,2,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,-1,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{ZY} & =y-z \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,4⟩-⟨-1,2,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-2,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{ZX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{ZY}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{ZX}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{ZY}}{|\\overset{\\to }{ZX}||\\overset{\\to }{ZY}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)\\cdot 0+(-1)\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot 6}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{6}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{40}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{240}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{4\\sqrt{15}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{15}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{15}})={25}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269101 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a087e7bc-4e74-584d-af3b-bf6bee4b75ea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Their Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f7ff979-0782-51f8-ae4c-e18fb9d4d5b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{90}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269103} {:answer/id #uuid "e2865549-e3e9-581d-a55a-ef32150ac727" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45.78}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269104} {:answer/id #uuid "501c6352-5d0e-5e87-bb7c-213d1c3cb56e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{32.88}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269105} {:answer/id #uuid "93c83d58-c4a8-534d-8989-eefb264493b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{36.87}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269106} {:answer/id #uuid "fcf16502-501f-5824-9c6f-c47d81fd150d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{33.74}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269107}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93c83d58-c4a8-534d-8989-eefb264493b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{36.87}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269106} :answer-field/id #uuid "a29ee5d9-bc93-5485-87d5-05b0c023178b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269102}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a459d13d-af6a-517a-94fc-980ae982205d" :question/math-academy-id "q-19027" :question/problem "Find the angle between $a=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 4+4\\cdot 2}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}}\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{\\sqrt{20}\\cdot \\sqrt{20}} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{4}{5})≈{36.87}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186325345 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a087e7bc-4e74-584d-af3b-bf6bee4b75ea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Their Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5bec37f1-5c4f-5b18-849a-dac4ba3e139a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{60}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325347} {:answer/id #uuid "43f0e300-ab89-572f-aa42-f3823226a421" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{90}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325348} {:answer/id #uuid "1a3deab4-c5ca-50d5-b1ca-8d0478828152" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325349} {:answer/id #uuid "c1abf405-e4b4-5787-bd09-52c38e51affb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325350} {:answer/id #uuid "e7165c27-7e55-560f-8bea-0c7b949d6c14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325351}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43f0e300-ab89-572f-aa42-f3823226a421" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{90}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325348} :answer-field/id #uuid "094225c0-1bf5-5991-b0a5-0f5a985b0491" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325346}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0336c98c-ed27-5cb7-8993-b9b1a36d3253" :question/math-academy-id "q-19028" :question/problem "Find the angle between $a=⟨3,4⟩$ and $b=⟨-4,3⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot (-4)+4\\cdot 3}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}}\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{\\sqrt{25}\\cdot \\sqrt{25}} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(0)={90}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186325352 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a418d9aa-d74d-58b1-a4c9-819f63593d50" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given the Value of Their Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a48530c6-5151-5767-8d33-b9b385ac683b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{46.18}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325354} {:answer/id #uuid "e0b19f68-2650-526f-9f23-98b81778f5c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{52.33}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325355} {:answer/id #uuid "d9a2d70f-606d-53d8-888c-2ef44dcc4886" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{37.75}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325356} {:answer/id #uuid "c1f2d9ac-ab27-5537-88a9-ae6bb04c1126" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{42.27}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325357} {:answer/id #uuid "5621eec5-b695-5579-abef-41be75308fd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{33.74}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325358}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1f2d9ac-ab27-5537-88a9-ae6bb04c1126" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{42.27}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325357} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffcb5a00-9fa0-5f57-8dd7-870c04f9bd64" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325353}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "30394f5f-9572-5a4f-bf32-50670ecbcc6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-19032" :question/problem "Given that $c\\cdot d=11$, find the angle between $c=⟨2t,1⟩$ and $d=⟨2,3⟩.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "First, since $c\\cdot d=11$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot d & =11 \\\\ 2t\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 3 & =11 \\\\ 4t+3 & =11 \\\\ 4t & =8 \\\\ t & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =⟨2(2),1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $c$ and $d$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{c\\cdot d}{|\\,c\\,||\\,d\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{x}{d}_{x}+{c}_{y}{d}_{y}}{\\sqrt{{c}_{x}^{2}+{c}_{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{{d}_{x}^{2}+{d}_{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{17}\\cdot \\sqrt{13}} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{221}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{221}})≈{42.27}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269115 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a087e7bc-4e74-584d-af3b-bf6bee4b75ea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Their Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2af7d00d-5eee-555a-9c9d-addb6f4e2953" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{7.84}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269117} {:answer/id #uuid "1c9fcf50-d78e-5968-97ce-3650cab4860b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{9.21}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269118} {:answer/id #uuid "d0615396-aa63-5291-a7c9-bc4f6e1a54b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{11.49}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269119} {:answer/id #uuid "6373f1ff-8af8-58d2-9b25-2bcc48548f47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{15.36}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269120} {:answer/id #uuid "a84efaa8-d771-5a5e-b71c-c2a53b44a9ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{35.92}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269121}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0615396-aa63-5291-a7c9-bc4f6e1a54b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{11.49}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269119} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7c79751-db81-5814-a47f-b1052c81c40b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269116}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9977a1dd-4a81-52ff-bede-89adf3e6a78e" :question/math-academy-id "q-19037" :question/problem "Find the angle between $a=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot (-1)+3\\cdot 2}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{3}^{2}}\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{14}\\cdot \\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{3\\sqrt{14}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{11}{3\\sqrt{14}})≈{11.49}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186325359 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a418d9aa-d74d-58b1-a4c9-819f63593d50" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given the Value of Their Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67a0e966-c4f3-560d-8ed6-ac3135eefe27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{88.29}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325361} {:answer/id #uuid "70b0e40d-efb1-50f0-bdc0-78ddb04a6a87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{67.48}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325362} {:answer/id #uuid "1a7c0d34-89b3-51f8-aa99-3d40a4d6cc25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{93.32}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325363} {:answer/id #uuid "fc63e80c-1a01-58e7-812c-d1b232e8a92a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{81.64}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325364} {:answer/id #uuid "09107298-68c8-5bea-a9c3-3569be3257a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{52.15}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325365}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc63e80c-1a01-58e7-812c-d1b232e8a92a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{81.64}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325364} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b70f907-71bb-5dc4-9e01-8a31caff20d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325360}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b85d2bd6-f159-5eda-95b8-8ed7b380eebb" :question/math-academy-id "q-19119" :question/problem "Consider the points $D(1,3,2)$, $E(t,2,4)$ and $F(3,t,3).$ Find $∠EDF$ given that $\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{DF}=2.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $D$, $E$, $F$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d=⟨1,\\,3,\\,2⟩,\\,e=⟨t,\\,2,\\,4⟩,\\,f=⟨3,\\,t,\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△DEF$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠EDF=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/assets/c9cfb3e84e6f76d243125f2a09246b2a1300a0134e71359bb2b528082f064f93.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{DE}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{DF}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE} & =e-d \\\\  & =⟨t,\\,2,\\,4⟩-⟨1,\\,3,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t-1,\\,-1,\\,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =f-d \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,t,\\,3⟩-⟨1,\\,3,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,t-3,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{DF}=2$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =2 \\\\ (t-1)\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot (t-3)+2\\cdot 1 & =2 \\\\ 2t-2-t+3+2 & =2 \\\\ t & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE} & =⟨-1-1,-1,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,-1,2⟩, \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =⟨2,-1-3,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-4,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{DE}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{DF}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{DF}}{|\\overset{\\to }{DE}||\\overset{\\to }{DF}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{9}\\cdot \\sqrt{21}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3\\sqrt{21}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{2}{3\\sqrt{21}})≈{81.64}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186325366 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7b1b8dc-bb50-59b4-8716-bdd6fbeada4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Three Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ab0f59e-5662-5943-95cb-331b97e423ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{90}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325368} {:answer/id #uuid "f0107953-55fc-5db8-8fd3-270eb966b147" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{180}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325369} {:answer/id #uuid "8de510b8-8eaf-5e4e-8b22-a2ca29bb7766" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325370} {:answer/id #uuid "f7812e21-c38a-5718-ad93-9ebb5f4389aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325371} {:answer/id #uuid "463db236-d16b-5282-aa3f-6b049c656135" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{120}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325372}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0107953-55fc-5db8-8fd3-270eb966b147" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{180}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325369} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fc88583-440a-5429-bf11-adc4beff062b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325367}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8202d480-d11e-56b0-8904-661a796de5e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-69828" :question/problem "Find $∠PQR$ given the points $P(-3,0,-1)$, $Q(-1,1,0)$, and $R(1,2,1).$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $P$, $Q$, $R$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p=⟨-3,0,-1⟩,\\,q=⟨-1,1,0⟩,\\,r=⟨1,2,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $△PQR$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠PQR=\\theta .$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/assets/209d43a5aab5d57fbd4cd7b421d41f0fa85bc58cfdd36251a8acf392b0ba7312.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{QP}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{QR}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{QP} & =p-q \\\\  & =⟨-3,0,-1⟩-⟨-1,1,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,-1,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{QR} & =r-q \\\\  & =⟨1,2,1⟩-⟨-1,1,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{QP}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{QR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{QP}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{QR}}{|\\overset{\\to }{QP}||\\overset{\\to }{QR}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2)\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-6}{\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-1)={180}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269136 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7b1b8dc-bb50-59b4-8716-bdd6fbeada4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Three Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "853ea703-1d96-539c-87e3-e34d3d095438" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{90}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269138} {:answer/id #uuid "d0f223ca-0fea-5bae-8cdd-b11ad4571b15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{27}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269139} {:answer/id #uuid "12fb3ba3-823c-5cfc-b083-6ce78c505fcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{88}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269140} {:answer/id #uuid "e05e7500-7274-5b9b-90bd-0b84dc643510" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{63}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269141} {:answer/id #uuid "9a09a8bd-4160-5cba-b8e6-8131c8959abe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{57}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269142}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e05e7500-7274-5b9b-90bd-0b84dc643510" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{63}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269141} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4556650-d240-5520-9d69-8f8ef1163437" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269137}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e553e89a-b69b-5299-b9b3-9573916538d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-69831" :question/problem "Find $∠QPR$ given the points $P(2,1,2)$, $Q(1,3,2)$, and $R(4,5,-2).$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $P$, $Q$, $R$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p=⟨2,1,2⟩,\\,q=⟨1,3,2⟩,\\,r=⟨4,5,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△PQR$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠QPR=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/assets/3003f0cb329a8f8ef9bc315c70df4773ac1f0c54843dea1208c68bd0f6227bd1.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =⟨1,3,2⟩-⟨2,1,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,2,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =⟨4,5,-2⟩-⟨2,1,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,4,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{PR}}{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}||\\overset{\\to }{PR}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 4+0\\cdot (-4)}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{6\\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5})≈{63}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299818 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7b1b8dc-bb50-59b4-8716-bdd6fbeada4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given Three Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc682e91-ae05-504d-a75b-61df41993129" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{60}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299820} {:answer/id #uuid "22262f06-d52f-5b38-9f64-4a78a1175669" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{90}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299821} {:answer/id #uuid "1fb860fa-84e4-5dea-9b77-02ffed6d22d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299822} {:answer/id #uuid "9b4845f1-3f57-5b30-8bbb-1c0151018f10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299823} {:answer/id #uuid "5262afc4-ebbd-5669-be2f-f42e39724e0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{120}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299824}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1fb860fa-84e4-5dea-9b77-02ffed6d22d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299822} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c26df84-5374-5583-8294-99ed982e65e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299819}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6dd6f17b-7e99-5c2a-8be5-e863ab15158a" :question/math-academy-id "q-69833" :question/problem "Find $∠XZY$ given the points $X(-1,0,3)$, $Y(-2,2,3)$, and $Z(-2,-1,3).$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $X$, $Y$, $Z$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=⟨-1,0,3⟩,\\,y=⟨-2,2,3⟩,\\,z=⟨-2,-1,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $△XYZ$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠XZY=\\theta .$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/assets/87453fecb9da6b9e673ab5a85a289a3fac73f4fb90fc8f1b33e7c0a80b1ea77f.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{ZX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{ZY}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{ZX} & =x-z \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,3⟩-⟨-2,-1,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,1,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{ZY} & =y-z \\\\  & =⟨-2,2,3⟩-⟨-2,-1,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,3,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{ZX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{ZY}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{ZX}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{ZY}}{|\\overset{\\to }{ZX}||\\overset{\\to }{ZY}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 3+0\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{3}^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}})={45}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269150 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a418d9aa-d74d-58b1-a4c9-819f63593d50" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Angle Between Two Vectors Given the Value of Their Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb9d024a-612a-5b88-b561-2eca5dd12c41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{65}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269152} {:answer/id #uuid "4ee2a05a-ca70-5223-ba9e-36cd6fa08e55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{79}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269153} {:answer/id #uuid "6eaac85c-277b-51f1-baf6-a4d8434347b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{82}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269154} {:answer/id #uuid "a4eef7ee-ce27-568c-aa25-74f1486ec107" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{58}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269155} {:answer/id #uuid "3f8ec3a5-7e51-5c63-9ee0-131bcdf218d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{75}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269156}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f8ec3a5-7e51-5c63-9ee0-131bcdf218d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{75}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269156} :answer-field/id #uuid "89db74db-3d63-59f5-b41d-544e3f33dabd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269151}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "61191758-28d5-55a6-95f0-ed679272a908" :question/math-academy-id "q-77164" :question/problem "Consider the points $A(3t,t,4),$ $B(3t,4t,3)$ and $C(5t,t+1,5).$ Find $∠BAC$ given that $\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}=2.$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A,$ $B$ and $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨3t,\\,t,\\,4⟩,\\,b=⟨3t,\\,4t,\\,3⟩,\\,c=⟨5t,\\,t+1,\\,5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045824/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨3t,\\,4t,\\,3⟩-⟨3t,\\,t,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,3t,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨5t,\\,t+1,\\,5⟩-⟨3t,\\,t,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}=2$, we can solve for $t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =2 \\\\ 0\\cdot 2t+3t\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 1 & =2 \\\\ 3t-1 & =2 \\\\ 3t & =3 \\\\ t & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨0,3,-1⟩, \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =⟨2,\\,1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{10}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{2\\sqrt{15}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{15}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{15}})≈{75}^{∘}.\n$$"}]}
